fresh-eyes: two adversarial review rounds, eight independent agents, on CONTRIBUTING/AGENTS/SECURITY and the gate config.

Round one: five lenses (gold-standard exemplars, ASD-STE100 line-by-line, factual accuracy against source, AI-writing patterns, three-persona walkthrough). Verdict three rewrite, two needs-edit. Twelve substantive defects, most of them repository behaviour asserted from CLI help text instead of read from source.

Round two, on the rewrite: verified ten of twelve defects fixed, found three the rewrite introduced, and established from gaff src/cli.rs run_ci that the pull_request trigger cannot turn the gate green. That finding was re-verified independently before acting on it. Filed as nk4l.

Mutation: not applicable. The change adds no guard, no branch, and no test. It is documentation, a workflow trigger, and package metadata. merge-gate.sh states that a note reading no mutation passes, so this records the reason rather than the word. The behavioural claims were verified instead: eight assertions in the rewritten documents were each checked against the gate scripts, the generated workflow, src/, and the GitHub API. The pull-request claim failed that check and the document now states the limit.

Gap: the ASD-STE100 lens agent died mid-response in round two, so voice compliance on the rewrite is unverified.
